pack UiEditor {
  format: "raepack"
  version: 1
  defaultTarget: compiled
  name: "UI Editor — .raescene viewer"
  description: "Opens ANY .raescene file and shows it as lib/ui renders it: the scene named by the first program argument (rae run ... -- path/to/scene.raescene), else RAE_UI_EDITOR_SCENE, else the shipped MainMenu sample. A desktop editor window (1400x900, resizable): a top bar, a left panel (project scenes, hierarchy, diagnostics), the edit area in the middle where the document is fitted and zoomed, a right inspector panel, a status bar — the chrome is authored in points in its own .raescene (H hides it, the top-bar toggles minimise the panels); the document keeps its own design frame. A scene's root-relative package path is its identity; sub-scenes resolve from the opened scene root (or --scene-root). Open a .raepack instead and its directory IS the root (the rae run --project semantics): every .raescene under it is listed in the chrome's project panel (P) and a tap opens it in place; --scene <package/Path> picks the first one. O (or the Open pill) shows the OS file picker; its choice goes through the same opener as the argument. G toggles the dashed frame + safe-area guides (an authored overlay scene). The wheel zooms the document about the cursor, a middle drag pans it, the top bar's zoom pill steps and resets. No chdir, ever. Theme tokens, textures and fonts come only through the scene's own blocks and its `import` list (#1008); whatever cannot load is a visible diagnostic, never a crash. Version 1 is a passive viewer; watching and the inspector follow."
  category: "UI"
  featured: "true"
  display: {
    width: 540
    height: 960
  }
  targets: {
    target compiled: {
      label: "Compiled"
      entry: "Main.rae"
      sources: {
        source: {
          path: "."
          emit: compiled
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
